nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","sent":"2026-11-13T17:57:00-08:00"}],"sent":"2026-11-14T01:05:00-08:00","effective":"2026-11-14T01:05:00-08:00","onset":"2026-11-14T01:05:00-08:00","expires":"2026-11-14T18:00:00-08:00","ends":"2026-11-15T04:00:00-08:00","status":"Actual","messageType":"Update","category":"Met","severity":"Moderate","certainty":"Likely","urgency":"Expected","event":"High Surf Warning","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS San Francisco CA","headline":"High Surf Warning issued November 14 at 1:05AM PST until November 15 at 4:00AM PST by NWS San Francisco CA","description":"* WHAT...For the High Surf Warning, dangerously large breaking\nwaves of 25 to 35 ft, with occasional sets of 40 to 50 ft at\nfavored breakpoints. For the Coastal Flood Advisory, large\nbreaking waves will run up beaches and crash over seawalls,\ninundating adjacent, low-lying infrastructure.\n\n* WHERE...All Pacific Coast Beaches.\n\n* WHEN...For the High Surf Warning, until 4 AM PST Sunday. For the\nCoastal Flood Advisory, now through 6 PM PST today.\n\n* IMPACTS...High tides will result in flooding of low-lying\ninfrastructure, isolated road closures, and coastal erosion.\nRising tides will bring water and waves farther up the beach\nthan normal, restricting escape from beaches and coastal\nareas. Dangerously large breaking waves can overpower\nswimmers, pulling people into the sea from beaches, jetties,\nand rocks resulting in significant physical injury and\nincreasing the risk of drowning. Waves can sweep across the\nshoreline without warning, pulling people into the sea from\nbeaches, jetties, and rocks.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...The Coastal Flood Advisory today is\nspecifically for the Pacific Coast, where large breaking waves\nwill spill over sea walls and run up beaches onto adjacent\ninfrastructure.","instruction":"If travel is required, allow extra time as some roads may be\nclosed. Do not drive around barricades or through water of\nunknown depth. Take the necessary actions to protect flood-prone\nproperty.\n\nEveryone should remain out of the water due to life-threatening\nsurf conditions. Stay off of jetties, piers, and other waterside\ninfrastructure.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["CFWMTR"],"WMOidentifier":["WHUS46 KMTR 140905"],"NWSheadline":["HIGH SURF WARNING REMAINS IN EFFECT UNTIL 4 AM PST SUNDAY... ...COASTAL FLOOD ADVISORY REMAINS IN EFFECT UNTIL 6 PM PST THIS EVENING"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"VTEC":["/O.CON.KMTR.SU.W.0001.000000T0000Z-261115T1200Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-11-15T04:00:00-08:00"],"expiredReferences":["w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.0632cb6f5b2eb910c29e12ac4f87fc7c178b0297.003.1,2026-11-13T15:53:00-08:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.0632cb6f5b2eb910c29e12ac4f87fc7c178b0297.001.2,2026-11-13T15:53:00-08:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f44cdf38b306227a23905cf0f5ed5f8d4854fc84.002.1,2026-11-13T03:44:00-08:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f44cdf38b306227a23905cf0f5ed5f8d4854fc84.001.1,2026-11-13T03:44:00-08:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.cdad9736fd52c00007a734100826b65a2f4993b4.002.1,2026-11-12T14:58:00-08:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.cdad9736fd52c00007a734100826b65a2f4993b4.001.1,2026-11-12T14:58:00-08:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f24acdc8bab05264fb6a2dc1481bf8cf8e0da56e.002.2,2026-11-11T22:48:00-08:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.f24acdc8bab05264fb6a2dc1481bf8cf8e0da56e.001.2,2026-11-11T22:48:00-08:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.dcd2d95d071b65ff14157dcba880a1162d3288fc.001.1,2026-11-11T18:09:00-08:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.dcd2d95d071b65ff14157dcba880a1162d3288fc.002.1,2026-11-11T18:09:00-08:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.4b5be439c18dd1d2d8f62b3a64cbb95f0f6a1b66.002.1,2026-11-11T08:08:00-08:00 w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov,urn:oid:2.49.0.1